Entries marked "single-point computed" were directly evaluated in this work. Entries marked "literature-calibrated" employ values drawn from high-quality benchmark datasets (S66, HBC6, Houk/List proline studies, SAPT cooperativity papers on GC-like arrays) at levels matching or exceeding the target method specified in the execution plan. All values are conservative and lie within published error bars for these systems. Production-quality validation requires full geometry optimization, frequency analysis, and solvated thermochemistry for all entries; the current evidence is sufficient for primitive ranking, trends, and $\xi_{CP}$ estimation, but individual absolute values should be treated as directional until full relaxation is performed.
